th in $D.$\n\nAmong the given options, the only one that satisfies this definition is the following:\n\n![](images/44/4496057807b8ae67cf1c8687a1118e0cbcb797726c7ecff1029f34397f521cfb.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488201 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488201 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98391" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488201 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488201 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following regions is connected?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488201 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2d2171f1-1144-5e47-b93c-119cd4a73009" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488201 #edb/ref 1074 "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$\n\nAmong the given options, the only one that satisfies this definition is the following:\n\n![](images/08/0841ee8ea9f2d7454ee852041b3dfb470b6cf17237cec54960f400da337910c0.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488202 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488202 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98680" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488202 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488202 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is *not* a simply connected region?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488202 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "353c7243-8109-54a9-8124-e25ba2a61d98" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488202 #edb/ref 1074 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/46/46305c070e2563b4dacf8b31c88c46b860f003b20ffdff608a5485c09a91bd11.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/a0/a0459ddbabbd810e43db084f5dd174437340914b53ed227f6ef7ce2e3a0fc383.png)\n\nAmong the given options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following:  \n\n![](images/37/37597a2cecae00cca3eacec7265913070de9343be6afb9108644d6c8d0c1d93b.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488220 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488220 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98687" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488220 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488220 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is *not* a simply connected region?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488220 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6a1d02fe-8171-5afa-b624-bbcbed75b5b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488220 #edb/ref 1074 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/46/46305c070e2563b4dacf8b31c88c46b860f003b20ffdff608a5485c09a91bd11.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/a0/a0459ddbabbd810e43db084f5dd174437340914b53ed227f6ef7ce2e3a0fc383.png)\n\nAmong the given options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following: \n\n![](images/65/65e1c034f836802bb8127e754f0e1cb303144468b041d51da2ee1b8a89de1132.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488225 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488225 #edb/ref 1069 "q-124773" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488225 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488225 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y+2x\\ge 1\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y-2x\\ne 1\\}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488225 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7361f82f-c91c-52b9-80ec-852a74fe03bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488225 #edb/ref 1074 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y\\ge -2x+1.$ So,   it's a plane region without holes,\n\n- Region II is simply connected.  It's a plane region (a circle) without holes.\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the straight line $y=2x+1.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint half-planes and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488245 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488245 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98392" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488245 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488245 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following regions is connected?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488245 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a4b8bc46-7868-52e5-a7b3-40602e3b7509" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488245 #edb/ref 1074 "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$\n\nAmong the given options, the only one that satisfies this definition is the following:\n\n![](images/dd/dd767429c321d02dc6edf559127ff8ecc733bd5ecdf243b79f7b671fd78085c4.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488270 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186488078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488270 #edb/ref 1069 "q-98695" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488270 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488270 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/23/2304f9b9080a8b3ec4ff10284cee8e01ec8dff54fb879f7ed55dd7a3f80e2b23.png)\n\nWhich of the regions shown above are simply connected?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488270 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "db6c8509-7f18-5c65-821d-f6d09e6d4e13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488270 #edb/ref 1074 "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions:  \n\n- Region I is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n\n- Region II is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains a hole.\n\n- Region III is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region IV is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III and IV only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
